findings.claim:
(e) You cannot close an open block by tapping it today. The open block's own bar is hidden by CSS, and cvPairSwap returns early when the tapped block is already big. The only ways to change what is open are opening another block, or closing the whole cog: a second cog tap, the backdrop, Cancel, Apply, Escape or App settings. Open/closed is decided entirely by the cv-fr-big / cv-ed-big classes, set in cvPairApply. Building a 'none' state and tap-to-close means four things:
- a new class, e.g. cv-none, in cvPairBig/cvPairApply;
- CSS that shows every bar, including the open block's own bar, as a header;
- a toggle in place of the early return at 8540;
- a decision on what opening the cog writes or reads in fm.cvPair.

clauses.build:
In edSwitch(big) (js/app.js:8395-8413), branch on !big. The small switch gets:
- .ed-l-s holding the Simple icon SVG and .ed-l-f holding the Full icon SVG (24 viewBox, stroke-width 1.8, drawn at 20px);
- no '⇄' glyph, because the sliding knob already says 'switch'.

The big switch inside the explanation keeps its words, 'Simple ⇄ Full', and 'You're in Full'.

aria-label and title stay action-named ('Switch to Simple editor'), so a screen reader and a PC hover still get words.

CSS (styles.css:8654-8683): the small switch shrinks from about 146px to about 84px:
- each half 40px;
- .ed-l from 58px to 40px;
- the knob's translateX from 78px to about 40px;
- the big switch's 88/108px left alone.

The icon is the chosen option (A recommended, see icon_options). It ships as inline SVG strings in app.js beside ED_ICON (8390), because the app has no icon set. FU7's `#cv-editor .ed-sw` stays visible.

